 "scope": "Review data for the proposal D28: replace the comparison rule of D19 (curvature ratio with a band) by the minimum of the one-loop effective potential Gamma(phi) = E_cl + E_zp on the relaxed soft path. Not adopted; the code of select_on_manifold is unchanged.",
 "script": "examples/nbcp_effective_potential_check.py",
 "principle": "Gamma(phi) is the one-loop (LSWT-order) effective potential of the soft coordinate phi: the classical energy minimized over all other coordinates at fixed phi, plus the harmonic zero-point energy about that constrained configuration. Only the torque along the orbit remains on this path; a torque transverse to the spins does not change H2, so dropping the linear term is the constrained one-loop calculation. For a flat classical orbit Gamma = const + E_zp, i.e. D17. Only phi is moved, so the O(1/S) relaxation of hard coordinates excluded by D18 does not enter. Validity requires adiabatic separation: curvature of Gamma small against the hard-mode stiffness.",
 "references": [
  "Shender, Sov. Phys. JETP 56, 178 (1982)",
  "Henley, PRL 62, 2056 (1989)",
  "Rau, McClarty, Moessner, PRL 121, 237201 (2018)",
  "Coleman and Weinberg, PRD 7, 1888 (1973)"
 ],
 "findings": [
  "D17 limit: at zero tilt the minimum of Gamma equals the D17 selection (Y: 3.7e-7 rad; V: 0), rigid and relaxed paths agree.",
  "The rigid orbit R_n(phi) overestimates classical pinning: Y at 1.7 degrees has a classical span of 7.5e-6 meV on the rigid orbit but 5.3e-7 meV on the relaxed path (factor 14), because the rigid rotation forbids the canting response to the in-plane field.",
  "Correction of the provisional statement (rigid orbit) that 1.7 degrees of field misalignment lets classical pinning win for Y at 0.2 T: on the relaxed path the minimum of Gamma stays 8.9e-3 rad from the quantum minimum.",
  "Y has no in-plane net moment: the relaxed classical span grows as tilt^2 (5.9e-10, 5.9e-8, 5.8e-6 meV at 0.001, 0.01, 0.1). V has an in-plane moment: the span grows linearly (1.8e-4, 5.4e-4 meV at 0.01, 0.03) and classical pinning dominates already at 0.57 degrees.",
  "V at tilt 0.1 (5.7 degrees): the relaxation does not converge (transverse gradient 5.6e-2) and the adiabatic ratio is 2.4e3; the soft-path picture fails there (the V state is not a local minimum under this tilt), which the validity check reports.",
  "Adiabatic ratio: 1.1e-2 (Y, up to 1.7 degrees), 1.7e-1 (Y, 16.7 degrees), 1e-3 to 1.5e-2 (V, up to 1.7 degrees)."
 ],
